; onehotr_single_column_penalty_overflow: a constraint expansion validates
; its penalty scale factors before it emits terms, so an out-of-range factor
; raises whether or not the expansion goes on to emit a term that uses it.
;
; A 2x1 grid gives ONEHOTR exactly one column, so the pair loop that
; consumes 2 * penalty never runs. Rust computes the factor above the loop
; and raises; xqvm_py evaluated it lazily inside the loop and halted. Under
; the pallet that is an eight-instruction extrinsic that faults on one node
; version and succeeds on another.
;
; penalty = 2^62, so 2 * penalty = 2^63 is not representable while -penalty
; is -- the linear factor is fine and only the quadratic one is not.
;
; EQUALITY, ATLEAST and ATLEASTW already behaved this way on both VMs
; (see constraints/equality_penalty_overflow), so this makes all five
; expansion sites consistent rather than making ONEHOT the exception.

PUSH 2
BQMX r0

PUSH 2                     ; rows
PUSH 1                     ; cols
RESIZE r0

PUSH 0                     ; row
PUSH 4611686018427387904   ; penalty
ONEHOTR r0
HALT
